Why the SM-X710 port needs it
-----------------------------
The X710 boots with this warning on every boot:

	adreno 3d00000.gpu: supply vdd not found, using dummy regulator
	adreno 3d00000.gpu: supply vddcx not found, using dummy regulator
	platform 3d6a000.gmu: [drm:a6xx_gmu_acd_probe] *ERROR* Unable to send ACD state to AOSS
	------------[ cut here ]------------
	Unable to drop a managed device link reference
	WARNING: drivers/base/core.c:1020 at device_link_put_kref+0x38/0x108
	Workqueue: events_unbound deferred_probe_work_func
	Call trace:
	 device_link_put_kref+0x38/0x108 (P)
	 device_link_del+0x30/0x4c
	 a6xx_gmu_init+0x5e8/0x63c
	 a6xx_gpu_init+0x4b4/0x5dc
	 adreno_bind+0x160/0x1dc
	 msm_drm_init+0xf8/0x1b0
	 msm_gpu_probe+0x64/0x80
	 adreno_probe+0x44/0x6c
	 ...
	 deferred_probe_work_func+0x80/0xe0

Captured on real hardware in `reference/boot-tests/test-046-*` and
`test-047-*`, and reproduced in test-179 and test-183.

Root cause of the splat: `a6xx_gmu_init()` creates the GMU<->cxpd link with
only `DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME`.  Without `DL_FLAG_STATELESS` the link is a
*managed* link, so it is owned by the driver core and released automatically
when the consumer device is unbound.  `a6xx_gmu_init()` nevertheless calls
`device_link_del(link)` on its error path.  `device_link_put_kref()` then
takes the `!device_is_registered(link->consumer)` branch, the consumer is
still registered, and it warns instead of dropping the reference:

	if (device_link_test(link, DL_FLAG_STATELESS))
		kref_put(&link->kref, __device_link_del);
	else if (!device_is_registered(link->consumer))
		__device_link_del(&link->kref);
	else
		WARN(1, "Unable to drop a managed device link reference\n");

The consumer is a driverless virtual power-domain device ("cx"), so the
managed lifecycle does not map onto it, which is exactly the argument in the
upstream commit message.  Passing `DL_FLAG_STATELESS` makes the link
explicitly owned and deleted by the msm driver, which is what the code
already assumes.

This is an upstream bugfix that applies to any SoC reaching this error path,
not an X710-specific hack.  It is being carried as a separate backport so the
stall A/B stays attributable: it is the only kernel change in its commit.

Fixes: ead5d3e5eb37 ("drm/msm/a6xx: Vote for cx gdsc from gpu driver")
Signed-off-by: Akhil P Oommen <akhilpo@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
[ gts9wifi: backport to v7.2-rc3; no adaptation needed. ] 
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 1b44b9e21ad8..ec13b27feee7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -2196,7 +2196,8 @@ int a6xx_gmu_wrapper_init(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu, struct device_node *node)
 		goto err_mmio;
 	}
 
-	if (!device_link_add(gmu->dev, gmu->cxpd, DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME)) {
+	if (!device_link_add(gmu->dev, gmu->cxpd,
+			     DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME | DL_FLAG_STATELESS)) {
 		ret = -ENODEV;
 		goto detach_cxpd;
 	}
@@ -2377,7 +2378,8 @@ int a6xx_gmu_init(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu, struct device_node *node)
 		goto err_mmio;
 	}
 
-	link = device_link_add(gmu->dev, gmu->cxpd, DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME);
+	link = device_link_add(gmu->dev, gmu->cxpd,
+			       DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME | DL_FLAG_STATELESS);
 	if (!link) {
 		ret = -ENODEV;
 		goto detach_cxpd;
-- 
